# Clean Architecture — backend

`presentation -> infrastructure -> application -> domain`. Arrows never point the other way.

| Layer                 | May import                                         | Never                                     |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| `@app/domain`         | nothing                                            | `@nestjs/*`, other layers, IO             |
| `@app/application`    | `@app/domain`                                      | `@nestjs/*`, infrastructure, presentation |
| `@app/infrastructure` | domain, application, `@nestjs/common`, drivers     | presentation                              |
| `@app/presentation`   | all                                                | its own business logic                    |

- Always import another layer through its package (`@app/domain`), never via relative paths (`../../domain/...`).
- Everything another layer needs is exported from that layer's `index.ts`.
- Interfaces implemented by infrastructure are declared inward: repositories in `domain/repositories`, other services in `application/ports`. DI tokens live in `application/common/tokens.ts`.

```ts
// ❌ use case coupled to Nest and to a concrete implementation
@Injectable()
export class CreateUserUseCase {
  constructor(private readonly repo: InMemoryUserRepository) {}
}

// ✅ plain TS, depends on the domain interface
export class CreateUserUseCase {
  constructor(
    private readonly users: UserRepository,
    private readonly ids: IdGenerator,
  ) {}
}
```

- Entities are built with `Entity.create(...)` (validates invariants) and rehydrated with `Entity.restore(...)`.
- Errors: `DomainError` for invariants, `NotFoundError`/`ConflictError` in application. Never throw `HttpException` outside presentation.
